Flask Task Manager

Description

This is a Flask web application for task management with support for authentication,
    roles (user / admin), registration, editing, and viewing tasks.
The project implements basic logic for managing users and tasks through HTML templates
    and an SQLite database.

📁 Project Structure

C:\PythonProjects\Flask/
│── .venv/                 # Virtual environment
│── static/                # Static files (CSS, JS, images)
│   ├── css/               # CSS styles
│   │   └── style.css      # Main stylesheet
│── templates/             # HTML templates
│   ├── login.html          
│   ├── register.html
│   ├── tasks.html
│   ├── admin.html
│   ├── add_task.html
│   ├── edit_task.html
│   ├── index.html
│   └── welcome.html
│── test/                  # Automated tests
│   └── test_app.py        # Pytest tests for pages, login and registration
│── app.py                 # Main Flask application
│── database.py            # SQLite database handling
│── todo.db                # SQLite database file
│── .env                   # Environment configuration
│── .gitignore             # Git ignore file
│── requirements.txt       # Dependencies

⚙️ Installation

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # або .venv\Scripts\activate на Windows

Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt
Run the application:
flask run

🧪 Testing

The project uses pytest for automated testing.
Tests are stored in the test/ folder.

Run all tests:

pytest

Run tests with detailed output:

pytest -v

Current tests check:

- public pages: /, /login, /register, /index
- redirects from protected pages without login: /tasks, /add_task, /admin
- successful login
- failed login
- new user registration
- duplicate user registration

During tests, the application uses a separate temporary database:

test_todo.db

This helps avoid changing the main local database todo.db while running tests.

🔐 Authentication

The user enters a username and password.
If the role in the database is admin, redirect to /admin_board.
If the role is user, redirect to /tasks.
User data is stored in the session.

🧠 Database Structure

Users table: id, username, password, role
Tasks table: id, user_id, description, created_at, due_at, status, priority, done, FOREIGN KEY (user_id → users.id)


🛡️ Recommendations
Use werkzeug.security for password hashing.
Add CSRF protection via Flask-WTF.
Create decorators for role verification (@admin_required, @login_required).

